window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a013-05d15879dfdd44ab.json"]={sha256:"05d15879dfdd44abdd56084c8d45266126f90adbc9a5985870da56c57c535bcb",value:{"id":"a013","title":"金屬閘極功函數工程","titleEn":"Metal-gate work-function engineering","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["能帶與閘極","材料堆疊","選擇性加工","閾值與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Band alignment and gates","Material stacks","Selective processing","Threshold and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a013-stage01","order":1,"title":"能帶與閘極","titleEn":"Band alignment and gates","description":"在「能帶與閘極」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for band alignment and gates, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義真空功函數","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function","objective":"完成「定義真空功函數」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define vacuum work function, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：定義真空功函數。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define vacuum work function. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「定義真空功函數」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define vacuum work function and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「定義真空功函數」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define vacuum work function: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-01-k1","title":"定義真空功函數的原理","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function principle","text":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","textEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device."},{"id":"a013-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「定義真空功函數」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define vacuum work function?","options":["金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-01"],"title":"平帶條件","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions","objective":"完成「平帶條件」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：平帶條件。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw flat-band conditions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「平帶條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw flat-band conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「平帶條件」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-02-k1","title":"平帶條件的原理","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions principle","text":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","textEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge."},{"id":"a013-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「平帶條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw flat-band conditions?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-02"],"title":"NMOS 與 PMOS","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets","objective":"完成「NMOS 與 PMOS」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：NMOS 與 PMOS。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate NMOS and PMOS targets. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「NMOS 與 PMOS」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate nmos and pmos targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「NMOS 與 PMOS」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-03-k1","title":"NMOS 與 PMOS的原理","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets principle","text":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。","textEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."},{"id":"a013-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「NMOS 與 PMOS」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate nmos and pmos targets?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-03"],"title":"閘介電層串聯","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack","objective":"完成「閘介電層串聯」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘介電層串聯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include the dielectric stack. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘介電層串聯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include the dielectric stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘介電層串聯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-04-k1","title":"閘介電層串聯的原理","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack principle","text":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","textEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks."},{"id":"a013-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘介電層串聯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include the dielectric stack?","options":["相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-04"],"title":"閾值抽取定義","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction","objective":"完成「閾值抽取定義」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose threshold extraction, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值抽取定義。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose threshold extraction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閾值抽取定義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose threshold extraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值抽取定義」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose threshold extraction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-05-k1","title":"閾值抽取定義的原理","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction principle","text":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","textEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds."},{"id":"a013-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值抽取定義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose threshold extraction?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-05"],"title":"厚度空間預算","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness","objective":"完成「厚度空間預算」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：厚度空間預算。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget gate-stack thickness. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「厚度空間預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget gate-stack thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「厚度空間預算」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-06-k1","title":"厚度空間預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness principle","text":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。","textEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."},{"id":"a013-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「厚度空間預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget gate-stack thickness?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage02","order":2,"title":"材料堆疊","titleEn":"Material stacks","description":"在「材料堆疊」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for material stacks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-06"],"title":"薄金屬連續性","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity","objective":"完成「薄金屬連續性」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：薄金屬連續性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thin-metal continuity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「薄金屬連續性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thin-metal continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「薄金屬連續性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-07-k1","title":"薄金屬連續性的原理","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity principle","text":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","textEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous."},{"id":"a013-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「薄金屬連續性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thin-metal continuity?","options":["極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-07"],"title":"介面偶極形成","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles","objective":"完成「介面偶極形成」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介面偶極形成。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace interface dipoles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「介面偶極形成」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace interface dipoles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介面偶極形成」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-08-k1","title":"介面偶極形成的原理","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles principle","text":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","textEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts."},{"id":"a013-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介面偶極形成」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace interface dipoles?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Interface reactions can create additional band shifts.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-08"],"title":"氮含量與成分","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition","objective":"完成「氮含量與成分」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氮含量與成分。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare nitrogen and composition. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「氮含量與成分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare nitrogen and composition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氮含量與成分」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-09-k1","title":"氮含量與成分的原理","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition principle","text":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。","textEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."},{"id":"a013-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氮含量與成分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare nitrogen and composition?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-09"],"title":"晶粒與取向","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation","objective":"完成「晶粒與取向」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶粒與取向。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess grain orientation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶粒與取向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess grain orientation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶粒與取向」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-10-k1","title":"晶粒與取向的原理","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation principle","text":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","textEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences."},{"id":"a013-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶粒與取向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess grain orientation?","options":["多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-10"],"title":"沉積成核","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation","objective":"完成「沉積成核」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect nucleation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沉積成核。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect nucleation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「沉積成核」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect nucleation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沉積成核」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect nucleation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-11-k1","title":"沉積成核的原理","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation principle","text":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","textEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior."},{"id":"a013-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沉積成核」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect nucleation?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-11"],"title":"熱處理重分布","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution","objective":"完成「熱處理重分布」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱處理重分布。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track thermal redistribution. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「熱處理重分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track thermal redistribution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱處理重分布」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-12-k1","title":"熱處理重分布的原理","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution principle","text":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。","textEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱處理重分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track thermal redistribution?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."],"answer":2,"explanation":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage03","order":3,"title":"選擇性加工","titleEn":"Selective processing","description":"在「選擇性加工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for selective processing, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-12"],"title":"區域保護層","titleEn":"Plan regional protection","objective":"完成「區域保護層」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for plan regional protection, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：區域保護層。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan regional protection. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「區域保護層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan regional protection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「區域保護層」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for plan regional protection: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-13-k1","title":"區域保護層的原理","titleEn":"Plan regional protection principle","text":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","textEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「區域保護層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan regional protection?","options":["選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-13"],"title":"金屬回蝕","titleEn":"Assess metal recess","objective":"完成「金屬回蝕」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess metal recess, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬回蝕。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess metal recess. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬回蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess metal recess and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬回蝕」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess metal recess: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-14-k1","title":"金屬回蝕的原理","titleEn":"Assess metal recess principle","text":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","textEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage."},{"id":"a013-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬回蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess metal recess?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-14"],"title":"選擇性去除","titleEn":"Check selective removal","objective":"完成「選擇性去除」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for check selective removal, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性去除。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check selective removal. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「選擇性去除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check selective removal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性去除」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for check selective removal: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-15-k1","title":"選擇性去除的原理","titleEn":"Check selective removal principle","text":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。","textEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."},{"id":"a013-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性去除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check selective removal?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-15"],"title":"窄腔填充","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill","objective":"完成「窄腔填充」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：窄腔填充。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect narrow-cavity fill. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「窄腔填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect narrow-cavity fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「窄腔填充」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-16-k1","title":"窄腔填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill principle","text":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","textEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids."},{"id":"a013-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「窄腔填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect narrow-cavity fill?","options":["外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Premature closure can conceal internal voids.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-16"],"title":"閘極電阻","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance","objective":"完成「閘極電阻」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate gate resistance, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘極電阻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate gate resistance. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「閘極電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate gate resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘極電阻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate gate resistance: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-17-k1","title":"閘極電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance principle","text":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","textEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria."},{"id":"a013-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘極電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate gate resistance?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-17"],"title":"金屬殘留短路","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges","objective":"完成「金屬殘留短路」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬殘留短路。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 做一張閾值歸因表：列金屬功函數、介面電荷及通道摻雜三個可能原因；為各原因分別指定材料分析、C-V 或摻雜輪廓的辨別證據。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate residual-metal bridges. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Build a threshold-attribution table for metal work function, interface charge and channel doping. Assign discriminating materials, C-V or doping-profile evidence to each.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬殘留短路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate residual-metal bridges and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬殘留短路」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-18-k1","title":"金屬殘留短路的原理","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges principle","text":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。","textEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."},{"id":"a013-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬殘留短路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate residual-metal bridges?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage04","order":4,"title":"閾值與可靠度","titleEn":"Threshold and reliability","description":"在「閾值與可靠度」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for threshold and reliability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-18"],"title":"C-V 與 I-V","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V","objective":"完成「C-V 與 I-V」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：C-V 與 I-V。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check C-V and I-V. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「C-V 與 I-V」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check c-v and i-v and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「C-V 與 I-V」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-19-k1","title":"C-V 與 I-V的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V principle","text":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","textEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities."},{"id":"a013-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「C-V 與 I-V」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check c-v and i-v?","options":["兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-19"],"title":"閾值空間圖","titleEn":"Map threshold variation","objective":"完成「閾值空間圖」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for map threshold variation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值空間圖。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map threshold variation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閾值空間圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map threshold variation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值空間圖」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for map threshold variation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-20-k1","title":"閾值空間圖的原理","titleEn":"Map threshold variation principle","text":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","textEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures."},{"id":"a013-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值空間圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map threshold variation?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-20"],"title":"溫度依賴","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence","objective":"完成「溫度依賴」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度依賴。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare temperature dependence. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「溫度依賴」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare temperature dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度依賴」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-21-k1","title":"溫度依賴的原理","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence principle","text":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。","textEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."},{"id":"a013-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度依賴」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare temperature dependence?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-21"],"title":"偏壓老化","titleEn":"Track bias aging","objective":"完成「偏壓老化」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for track bias aging, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：偏壓老化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bias aging. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「偏壓老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bias aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「偏壓老化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for track bias aging: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-22-k1","title":"偏壓老化的原理","titleEn":"Track bias aging principle","text":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","textEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets."},{"id":"a013-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「偏壓老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bias aging?","options":["閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-22"],"title":"雙極性整合","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration","objective":"完成「雙極性整合」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：雙極性整合。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review dual-polarity integration. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「雙極性整合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review dual-polarity integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「雙極性整合」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-23-k1","title":"雙極性整合的原理","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration principle","text":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","textEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation."},{"id":"a013-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「雙極性整合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review dual-polarity integration?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-23"],"title":"金屬閘極驗收","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate","objective":"完成「金屬閘極驗收」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬閘極驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the metal gate. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「金屬閘極驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the metal gate and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬閘極驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-24-k1","title":"金屬閘極驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate principle","text":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。","textEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."},{"id":"a013-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬閘極驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the metal gate?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"}};
